# Shell scripts must stay LF: a CRLF shebang makes Linux and macOS look for an
# interpreter literally named "bash\r" and the script dies with exit 127.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Generated by pg_dump inside Docker (always LF). Pinning it stops a Windows
# checkout flipping it to CRLF and making check-reference.sh report a false diff.
scripts/schema-diff/artifacts/reference-schema.normalized.sql text eol=lf

# Java sources are stored with CRLF (282 files at the time of writing) and the local and CI
# whitespace checks use core.whitespace=cr-at-eol to match. Pin them as-is so a checkout on
# another platform cannot rewrite the line endings and produce a repo-wide phantom diff, and so
# an editor writing LF into a CRLF file shows up as a real change rather than noise. "-text"
# freezes the bytes: no normalization on commit, no conversion on checkout. Normalizing the tree
# to LF is a separate deliberate change, not something a clone should do silently.
*.java -text
